   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/PVES/Electroweak/ElectricCharge.lean",
   "fix": "Add the simp-normal `col` forms and tag them, e.g. `@[simp] theorem isospinT3_col (k) : isospinT3.col k = Pi.single k (isospinWeight k : \u2102)` and `@[simp] theorem electricChargeOperator_col (y k) : (electricChargeOperator y).col k = Pi.single k (doubletElectricCharge y k : \u2102)`, both immediate from `*_eq_diagonal` plus `Matrix.col_diagonal`; keep the `*_mulVec_single` forms for `rw` if wanted. Check whether the `doubletAction \u2026` version is then already closed by `simp` (via `doubletAction_electricChargeGenerator`) before tagging a third.",
   "issue": "`isospinT3_mulVec_single` (:241), `electricChargeOperator_mulVec_single` (:248) and `doubletAction_electricChargeGenerator_mulVec_single` (:255) state the eigenvalue results as `M *\u1d65 Pi.single k 1 = c \u2022 Pi.single k 1`. Mathlib's `@[simp] Matrix.mulVec_single` rewrites every such LHS to `M.col k`, after which none of the three lemmas applies by `rw` or `simp` and the file offers no `.col` lemma \u2014 the charge eigenvalues are reachable only if the consumer avoids `simp` entirely. This is the same stranding the author's own simpNF output demonstrates, not a reason to leave the lemmas as-is.",
